  "description": "T3. False Acacia. Mature heavily leaning tree in decline. Dieback throughout canopy and decay present at stem base. Fell to ground level via sectional takedown: Poison stump to prevent regrowth: Return to grind out stump in 2 months. Replant with a more suitable ornamental species in similar position 1 year after stump removal. T7 Eucalyptus. Semi mature tree previously reduced. To maintain cyclical pruning; Reduce canopy height by 3m and lateral spread by 2m. Shape and balance. CH 10 CS 7m PH 7m PS 5m T7a Silver Maple: Mature tree previously reduced. Colonized by wood decay fungus identified as Ganoderma applanatum at stem base. To mitigate failure; pollard to a safe height of 6m above ground level. T8. Cherry See plan Crown lift over access road by 2m. T8a. Birch See plan Crown lift over access road by 2m. T9. Silver Maple. Mature tree previously reduced. To maintain cyclical pruning; Reduce canopy height by 4m and lateral spread by 3m. Shape and balance. CH 11 CS 8m PH 7m PS 5m T10. Cherry. Mature tree previously reduced. To maintain cyclical pruning; Reduce canopy height by 2m and lateral spread by 2m. Shape and balance. CH 7 CS 7m PH 5m PS 5m",
